-- THE PERMUTED HALF of `record_xmod_field_order/`.  This is `zrmod.mdk`'s
-- declaration — fields `b` then `a` — under a module name that sorts FIRST instead
-- of last.
--
-- 🚨 WHY THE PAIR EXISTS AND WHY IT IS NAMES AND NOT IMPORT CLAUSES.  Pre-fix the
-- winner was `pairRecordByName (headL owners)` over `sortUniqS`ed owner keys, and
-- on the emit path every key is `<mid>__<ctor>` — so the decision followed module
-- NAME sort order.  Import-clause order is invariant to it, which is why permuting
-- the import clauses in `entry.mdk` would have produced a differential that passes
-- for the wrong reason.  Permuting the NAMES flips which module is the loser, so
-- this cell and its sibling fail in COMPLEMENTARY halves before the fix and must
-- both be fully correct after it.
public export data Cfg = { b : Int, a : Int }

mkAA : Cfg
mkAA = Cfg { b = 33, a = 44 }

-- projected INSIDE the declaring module: `b` is slot 0, `a` is slot 1.
export aaA : Int
aaA = mkAA.a

export aaB : Int
aaB = mkAA.b
